                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's just the same old Serious Sam repackaged yet another time. It plays more like the original than the HD remasters as kleers don't vault over each others and fly to your face. But they've added an extra campaign in this. It's not a very balanced campaign and some of the maps are outright bad, like that subterranean pyramid which felt like a chore to clear. The new weapons are crazy overpowered and the game was balanced around them. There's a corridor that's outright impossible on serious difficulty without alt fire blasting everything with the new mini rocket launcher as it makes the regular arsenal pale that much in comparison in close quarters. The regular old campaigns are still gold and the third one is a bit questionable.",
